Chapter: DtlsHandshakeTest
  cites Encode chapter DtlsHandshake

 The DTLS 1.3 handshake machine as an action trace (RFC 9147).

 This is the payoff of writing the machine as a pure step function: a
 datagram handshake, whose entire difficulty is loss and reordering, is
 tested here with no network, no peer, and no timing. We hand it events
 in an order a hostile network would produce and assert exactly what it
 decides to do.

Section: Formatting

  fmt-act : DtlsAction -> Text
  fmt-act (a) =
    when a
      is ActSend (f) -> "send" & show f
      is ActSetTimer (d) -> "timer" & show d
      is ActDeliverKeys -> "keys"
      is ActAck -> "ack"
      is ActAbort (x) -> "abort" & show x

  fmt-acts : List DtlsAction -> Text
  fmt-acts (as) = fmt-acts-loop as 0 (list-length as) ""

  fmt-acts-loop : List DtlsAction, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  fmt-acts-loop (as) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else if i == 0 then fmt-acts-loop as (i + 1) n (fmt-act (list-at as i))
    else fmt-acts-loop as (i + 1) n (acc & "," & fmt-act (list-at as i))

  fmt-phase : DtlsHsPhase -> Text
  fmt-phase (p) =
    when p
      is PhStart -> "start"
      is PhWaitServerHello -> "wait-sh"
      is PhWaitAck -> "wait-ack"
      is PhConnected -> "connected"
      is PhFailed -> "failed"

Section: Happy Path

 No loss, no cookie. The shortest handshake this machine can have.

  h1 : DtlsHsStep = dtls-hs-step dtls-hs-new (EvStart 0)
  h2 : DtlsHsStep = dtls-hs-step (h1.step-state) (EvServerFlight 50)
  h3 : DtlsHsStep = dtls-hs-step (h2.step-state) (EvAck 90)

  test-happy : Text =
    "hs happy: " & fmt-acts (h1.step-actions) & " | " & fmt-acts (h2.step-actions) & " | " & fmt-acts (h3.step-actions) & " | " & fmt-phase ((h3.step-state).hs-phase)

Section: Cookie Exchange

 The server refuses to allocate state until the client proves it can
 receive at the address it claims. The client answers the
 HelloRetryRequest with flight 3, and -- this is the part worth
 asserting -- the retransmission timer RESETS to 1000 for the new
 flight rather than carrying the old backoff forward.

  c1 : DtlsHsStep = dtls-hs-step dtls-hs-new (EvStart 0)
  c2 : DtlsHsStep = dtls-hs-step (c1.step-state) (EvTimeout 1000)
  c3 : DtlsHsStep = dtls-hs-step (c2.step-state) (EvHelloRetry [9, 9, 9, 9] 1200)

  test-cookie-flight : Text =
    "hs cookie: " & fmt-acts (c2.step-actions) & " | " & fmt-acts (c3.step-actions) & " | timer=" & show ((c3.step-state).hs-timer) & " retries=" & show ((c3.step-state).hs-retries)

Section: Retransmission Backoff

 RFC 9147 section 5.8.2: double at each retransmission, up to no less
 than 60 seconds. Ten timeouts from a 1000 ms start walk the timer
 1000 -> 2000 -> 4000 ... and then CLAMP at 60000 rather than running
 away.

  bo : List Integer = bo-loop dtls-hs-new 0 12 []

  bo-loop : DtlsHsState, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  bo-loop (st) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else if i == 0 then bo-loop ((dtls-hs-step st (EvStart 0)).step-state) (i + 1) n acc
    else bo-step st i n acc

  bo-step : DtlsHsState, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  bo-step (st) (i) (n) (acc) =
    let r = dtls-hs-step st (EvTimeout (i * 1000))
    in bo-loop (r.step-state) (i + 1) n (list-push acc ((r.step-state).hs-timer))

  test-backoff : Text =
    "hs backoff: " & fmt-ints bo

  fmt-ints : List Integer -> Text
  fmt-ints (xs) = fmt-ints-loop xs 0 (list-length xs) ""

  fmt-ints-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  fmt-ints-loop (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else if i == 0 then fmt-ints-loop xs (i + 1) n (show (list-at xs i))
    else fmt-ints-loop xs (i + 1) n (acc & "," & show (list-at xs i))

Section: Giving Up

 The RFC does not bound the retry count. Bare metal must: an unbounded
 retry against a black hole is a hang, and a hang on a device nobody can
 reach is the failure this project exists to prevent. After the bound the
 machine aborts and stays failed -- it does not quietly keep trying.

  g0 : DtlsHsState = (dtls-hs-step dtls-hs-new (EvStart 0)).step-state
  g1 : DtlsHsState = give-up-loop g0 0 10

  give-up-loop : DtlsHsState, Integer, Integer -> DtlsHsState
  give-up-loop (st) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then st
    else give-up-loop ((dtls-hs-step st (EvTimeout (i * 1000))).step-state) (i + 1) n



 After ten retries the machine is still trying (retries=10, timer clamped
 at 60000). The eleventh timeout is the one that gives up: it emits the
 abort and moves to failed. A twelfth changes nothing -- failed is
 terminal, and a machine that could be nudged out of it by a late packet
 would be a machine an attacker could restart.


  gfinal : DtlsHsStep = dtls-hs-step g1 (EvTimeout 99999)
  gafter : DtlsHsStep = dtls-hs-step (gfinal.step-state) (EvTimeout 111111)

  test-giveup : Text =
    "hs giveup: retries=" & show (g1.hs-retries) & " phase=" & fmt-phase (g1.hs-phase) & " then=" & fmt-acts (gfinal.step-actions) & "/" & fmt-phase ((gfinal.step-state).hs-phase) & " after=" & fmt-acts (gafter.step-actions) & "/" & fmt-phase ((gafter.step-state).hs-phase)

Section: Stale Timer After Connect

 A timer that fires after the handshake finished is normal on a lossy
 link. Re-arming on it would keep a finished connection retransmitting at
 a peer that has moved on, so a connected machine ignores it entirely.

  s1 : DtlsHsStep = dtls-hs-step (h3.step-state) (EvTimeout 5000)

  test-stale : Text =
    "hs stale: " & fmt-acts (s1.step-actions) & "/" & fmt-phase ((s1.step-state).hs-phase)

Section: Server Cookie Verdict

 Three outcomes and no fourth. A bad cookie MUST abort with
 illegal_parameter (47) -- it is not the same as no cookie, and quietly
 re-issuing a HelloRetryRequest would give an attacker an oracle and a
 free retry.

  sec : List Integer = [1, 2, 3, 4]
  addr : List Integer = [10, 0, 0, 7]
  good : List Integer = dtls-cookie sec addr
  bad : List Integer = list-set-at (dtls-cookie sec addr) 0 (bit-xor (list-at (dtls-cookie sec addr) 0) 1)

  test-verdict-none : Text =
    "hs verdict none=" & fmt-act (dtls-server-verdict sec addr [])

  test-verdict-good : Text =
    "hs verdict good=" & fmt-act (dtls-server-verdict sec addr good)

  test-verdict-bad : Text =
    "hs verdict bad=" & fmt-act (dtls-server-verdict sec addr bad)

 A cookie is bound to the address. The same secret and a different
 address must not verify, or the token is transferable and stops proving
 anything about who is on the other end.

  test-verdict-other-addr : Text =
    "hs verdict wrong-addr=" & fmt-act (dtls-server-verdict sec [10, 0, 0, 8] good)

Section: Anti-Amplification

 A server may send at most three times what it has received, before the
 address is verified. Without it DTLS is a reflector.

  test-amp : Text =
    "hs amp: at=" & show (dtls-amplification-ok 100 0 300) & " over=" & show (dtls-amplification-ok 100 0 301) & " partial=" & show (dtls-amplification-ok 100 250 50) & " budget=" & show (dtls-amplification-budget 100 250)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni test-happy
    print-line-uni test-cookie-flight
    print-line-uni test-backoff
    print-line-uni test-giveup
    print-line-uni test-stale
    print-line-uni test-verdict-none
    print-line-uni test-verdict-good
    print-line-uni test-verdict-bad
    print-line-uni test-verdict-other-addr
    print-line-uni test-amp
  end
